>Who all thinks that backed up save games is cheating?  [...]

I do.

>I say that I have no remorse because (a) By the time I care enough to
>dupe save files I've invested 10 hours or so in a character, 

To me, investing 10+ hours in a character, then losing him, is an
essential part of the game.  When I ascend (not that often... about once 
a year) I get a thrill from knowing that I beat the game on its own
terms.  If I back up and restore, I can ascend every time.  No thrill, 
though, because I had to cheat to win.

>(b) The
>game can crash unexpectedly, at any time, rubbing out a character that
>may have done nothing wrong, 

_IF_ you don't have restore on your system, or you don't have the privs 
to run restore, or if the crash wipes out the levels files, keeping _one_ 
backed up save file isn't cheating as long as you only use it to recover 
from a crash.  If you use it to recover from dying, that's cheating.

>and (c) I don't see how its any different
>from any other game that does have a save feature.

The terms of the game of Nethack include not being able to fall back
to a previously saved position.  The terms of those other games do 
include being able to fall back.  It's not cheating to abide by the 
terms of the game.  It's dishonest to claim that you won a game when
you used saved positions, but if the game allows it, it's not cheating.

>Is there anyone out there who finished any of the Ultima, King's Quest,
>Wizardry, SSI AD&D, Infocom, whatever games WITHOUT falling back upon
>a previously saved position?  

Yes.  

